<decision #track.simplify_codument_actions.defaults {
  priority = "P0"
  status = "accepted"
  durable_candidate = false
  confidence = 0.99
  reversibility = "moderate"
}
(
  <question ?>What should planning create by default and when should attractor checks run?</?>
  <recommendation ?>Always create design.md and decisions.xnl; keep durable folders on demand and make fresh attractor checks explicit or high-risk final-phase only.</?>
  <answer { }
  (
    <raw-answer ?>The user confirmed these defaults and requested lower attractor frequency without splitting the coding profile.</?>
    <decision-text ?>Planning creates design.md and decisions.xnl unconditionally, while decisions/ and memory/ are demand-created. Ordinary actions and phases do not run fresh attractor checks by default.</?>
    <rationale ?>This preserves durable planning context while avoiding repeated full-context review work.</?>
    <evidence ?>Mission decisions action_taxonomy, maintain_track, and attractor.</?>
  )
  >
)
>
